From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 09:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Do not use the on-device model service on Windows

Default OptimizationGuideOnDeviceModel to disabled on Windows, as on
other platforms without the service: the browser starts no
on_device_model utility (an AI model host, one more process and JIT
pool copy under Playport; PLA-394). Social Club replaces the browser's
--disable-features, so a switch cannot do this. Apply after the pinned
CEF stock patches.

Class: feature
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-18-cef-late-children.md
Offered-upstream: no
---
 .../core/optimization_guide_features.cc            |    6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/components/optimization_guide/core/optimization_guide_features.cc b/components/optimization_guide/core/optimization_guide_features.cc
index b75689a78a..92ab860d2c 100644
--- a/components/optimization_guide/core/optimization_guide_features.cc
+++ b/components/optimization_guide/core/optimization_guide_features.cc
@@ -95,10 +95,10 @@ BASE_FEATURE(kOptimizationGuidePredictionModelKillswitch,
 BASE_FEATURE(kOptimizationGuideModelExecution,
              base::FEATURE_ENABLED_BY_DEFAULT);
 
-// Whether to use the on device model service in optimization guide.
+// Whether to use the on device model service in optimization guide. Off on
+// Windows: no on_device_model utility process.
 BASE_FEATURE(kOptimizationGuideOnDeviceModel,
-#if BUILDFLAG(IS_WIN) || BUILDFLAG(IS_MAC) || BUILDFLAG(IS_LINUX) || \
-    BUILDFLAG(IS_CHROMEOS)
+#if BUILDFLAG(IS_MAC) || BUILDFLAG(IS_LINUX) || BUILDFLAG(IS_CHROMEOS)
              base::FEATURE_ENABLED_BY_DEFAULT);
 #else
              base::FEATURE_DISABLED_BY_DEFAULT);
